From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 13:34:25 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] Review: UW_JIT_KEEP_BUILD keeps a build without changing
 the kernels; the cache is checked before the discard

debug=True also adds a trace to every kernel, so it was a poor way to keep
the sources a run compiles; UW_JIT_KEEP_BUILD=1 keeps the build directory
and changes nothing else. test_0903 now asserts the module reached the disk
cache: a discard moved ahead of store_module would store nothing and send
every other rank to compile its own copy, and no test would have noticed.
The discard's docstring says what is lost (native frames in a kernel read
as ??, tracebacks lose cy_ext.pyx lines) and that on NFS an empty directory
stays per compile. test_0004 removes the build directories its debug=True
compiles keep.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
